NOTE:The only ship. It has no port\, there being no ports\, so it cannot b
 e visited\; it has no line\, so it cannot be rung\; and the post goes by 
 bottle\, which it has passed several times without stopping. This card is
  therefore for keeping and not for use. File it under C. It will be the o
 ne entry in your book that has never let a call go unanswered\, none havi
 ng arrived.\n\nThe number given is the masthead\, which is one character 
 high. The address is correct to the nearest sea. The birthday is the day 
 counting began\, which is as close as anyone got to a launch. Do not expe
 ct a card back. The Caret keeps no book\, knowing nobody\, and has never 
 mislaid a friend as a result.
